# Keep every text file on LF, in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# The windows-latest runner defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, so checkouts get
# CRLF. A step that regenerates a file with LF then makes `git status` report a
# modification even though the bytes are semantically identical — that is how
# `nodara-cli schema --out schema` kept flagging `schema/` as stale on CI while
# the same check was clean locally. Declaring `eol=lf` here overrides
# `core.autocrlf` for everything tracked, so a checkout and its generator agree.
* text=auto eol=lf
